Shader modules are not kept for every pipeline: a pipeline lets go of its modules once built, and
the shader reuse cache keeps at most EDEN_NX2_SHADER_REUSE_MIB (32) of SPIR-V, oldest keys first out.

The driver keeps a copy of the SPIR-V in each VkShaderModule. Every graphics pipeline held its
modules for good, and the reuse cache kept up to four variants of them for every translation key, so
they only grew: Eden's largest heap holder on Mario Kart World (110 MiB in 3,585 modules at 240 s,
growing with each pipeline a race builds). A key that left the reuse cache is translated again when
a pipeline needs it. ConfigureFunc reads the modules before the build is queued now, since the build
lets go of them.

